---
import ShareIcon from "@/assets/icons/share.svg"
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro"
import CampaignPartners from "@/components/CampaignPartners.astro"
import MetaPage from "@/components/MetaPage.astro"
import { campaignStatus } from "@/data/campaign"
---

<Layout
  sections={[
  { id: "problem", label: "What is at stake" },
  { id: "weg", label: "What we are doing" },
  { id: "handeln", label: "How you can help" },
  { id: "vision", label: "What we want to achieve" },
  { id: "position", label: "Who we are" },
]}
>
  <MetaPage
    slot="head"
    description="Financial privacy is a fundamental right. Bitcoin Austria is preparing a legal challenge to indiscriminate financial data collection under DAC8."
  />
  <article class="campaign landing">
    <header class="hero">
      <h1>
        Financial privacy is a fundamental right. <span>Let’s defend it.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="lead">
        You use your money to pay for medical treatment, support relatives or
        donate to a political cause. That is part of your private life.
        Financial privacy protects your freedom to make those choices without
        others scrutinising your personal life.
      </p>
      <p class="prose">
        Since 2026, crypto-asset providers in Austria have had to prepare
        financial data on all their customers for the tax authority, without any
        specific suspicion. We believe this collection under DAC8 violates
        fundamental rights and are preparing a legal challenge.
      </p>
      <nav class="hero-actions" aria-label="Get started">
        <a class="button primary" href="/en/donate/">Support the case</a>
        <a class="button" href="/en/background/">What DAC8 requires</a>
      </nav>
      <p class="campaign-status">
        <a href="/en/updates/">Austria · {campaignStatus.en.label}</a>
      </p>
      <dl class="keyfigures" aria-label="Key facts">
        <div>
          <dt>
            <strong>Customers</strong>
            are covered, even if their data is not ultimately reported.
          </dt>
          <dd>All</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>
            <strong>Retention by the provider</strong>
            of records documenting checks and reporting of your data.
          </dt>
          <dd>10 <small>years</small></dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>
            <strong>First report</strong>
            to the tax authority, covering the 2026 reporting year.
          </dt>
          <dd><time datetime="2027-07-31">31 July 2027</time></dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </header>
    <section id="problem" aria-labelledby="problem-heading">
      <h2 id="problem-heading">What is at stake</h2>
      <p class="section-intro">
        You can pay your taxes correctly and still want your finances to remain
        private. Information about your money can reveal details about your
        life. If it is shared, misunderstood or stolen, you bear the
        consequences.
      </p>
      <p class="prose">
        DAC8 is an EU directive on exchanging tax information. Reports contain
        identities and annual crypto-asset aggregates, not a list of individual
        payments. Over the years, even these aggregates create a financial
        profile.
      </p>
      <ul class="facts">
        <li>
          <strong>Everyone is covered, not just suspects.</strong>
          <p>
            Providers must prepare reporting data for all customers, including
            those who will not ultimately be reported. This requirement appears
            in Austrian law, not in the directive.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>A profile builds up over time.</strong>
          <p>
            Annual reports reveal activity. Providers may also retain links
            between names, wallet addresses and individual transactions. For
            people who pay with cryptocurrencies, these links can expose parts
            of everyday life.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>A data breach cannot be undone.</strong>
          <p>
            Stolen customer data can make people targets for extortion and
            robbery. According to France’s Gendarmerie, criminals use leaked
            data from a crypto tax service to select victims. Even mistaken
            assumptions about their wealth put them at risk.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Ten years instead of five.</strong>
          <p>
            Austrian law provides for reported crypto-asset data to be deleted
            after ten years, compared with five for corresponding bank-account
            data. The legislative materials do not explain the difference.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <a class="text-link" href="/en/background/#gemeldet"
        >What is reported, and what is not</a
      >
    </section>
    <section id="weg" aria-labelledby="weg-heading">
      <h2 id="weg-heading">What we are doing</h2>
      <p class="section-intro">{campaignStatus.en.text}</p>
      <p class="prose">
        The campaign against the retention of telephone and internet data is a
        precedent for resistance: in 2014, the Court of Justice struck down the
        directive and Austria’s Constitutional Court struck down the national
        law. That success shows that even sweeping surveillance laws can be
        changed.
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/en/background/#rechtsweg"
        >Our legal strategy in detail</a
      >
    </section>
    <section id="handeln" aria-labelledby="handeln-heading">
      <h2 id="handeln-heading">How you can help</h2>
      <ul class="facts action-facts">
        <li>
          <strong>Help fund the case</strong>
          <p>
            Your donation primarily helps cover the costs of the proceedings.
          </p>
          <a class="button primary" href="/en/donate/">Donate</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Follow the case</strong>
          <p>We publish news and next steps here and via RSS.</p>
          <a class="button" href="/en/updates/">Updates</a>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <button class="text-link" type="button" data-share>
        <ShareIcon />
        Share
      </button>
      <p class="share-status" data-share-status aria-live="polite"></p>
    </section>
    <section id="vision" aria-labelledby="vision-heading">
      <h2 id="vision-heading">What we want to achieve</h2>
      <p class="section-intro">
        A liberal democracy depends on freedom, privacy and the rule of law. For
        us, a red line is crossed when the state collects everyone’s financial
        data as a precaution, without specific suspicion. We want to roll back
        this indiscriminate surveillance.
      </p>
      <p class="prose">
        We consider targeted investigations based on specific suspicion
        necessary: with a legal basis, limited scope and independent oversight.
        Authorities must justify whose data they need and for what purpose. Mass
        surveillance reverses this principle: everyone is covered without
        specific suspicion against them.
      </p>
      <ul class="facts">
        <li>
          <strong>What we aim to achieve</strong>
          <p>
            Overturn disproportionate obligations, limit data collection and
            secure effective protection for those affected. We seek judicial
            scrutiny of the collection covering all customers, the reporting
            fields and the retention periods.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Why we are confident</strong>
          <p>
            We believe effective limits can be secured. That is why we combine
            concrete proceedings with political advocacy: in court and with the
            representatives who can change these laws.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>
    <section id="position" aria-labelledby="position-heading">
      <h2 id="position-heading">Who we are</h2>
      <p class="section-intro">
        dac8.org is an initiative by Bitcoin Austria, the nonprofit Bitcoin
        association founded in Vienna in 2011. We are Bitcoiners and
        cypherpunks. We see privacy as a prerequisite for a free society.
      </p>
      <p class="prose">
        We oppose indiscriminate collection of financial data, not taxation. The
        campaign concerns everyone covered by DAC8, regardless of which
        crypto-assets they use.
      </p>
      <p class="prose">
        Our campaign starts in Austria. DAC8 applies across the EU:
        organisations, businesses and experts who want to challenge the law in
        their country are welcome to contact us. We share arguments, sources and
        experience: <a href="mailto:kontakt@dac8.org">kontakt@dac8.org</a>
      </p>
      <CampaignPartners />
    </section>
  </article>
  <script>
    import { initializeShareButtons } from "@/lib/share"
    initializeShareButtons()
  </script>
</Layout>
